# Generated code — review, refactor, security tests

Agent/LLM patches are **untrusted until the gate passes**. Do not treat generated code as done after it compiles.

## Before commit / push

1. **Review** — read the diff. Check auth, credits, webhooks, untrusted JD/resume wrapping, and no secrets in Client Components (`jobbeagle-enterprise-security.mdc`).
2. **Refactor** — surgical types (no `any`), no leftover dump code, untrusted model inputs go through `wrapUntrusted` / `assembleAnalysisDocuments`.
3. **Security tests** — run `npm run gate:generated` (static patch review + `npm run test:security`).

If `gate:generated` prints `BLOCK`, fix and re-run. `REFACTOR` notes must be addressed when they are in `lib/` or `app/api/`.

CI job `generated-code-gate` runs the same command on every push/PR to `main`.
